{
  "_comment": "OPTION C — master-organizer.json stays lean; checklist lives in a separate per-ticket file.",
  "_tradeoffs": [
    "PROS: master-organizer.json stays small and fast to edit by hand — same shape as today",
    "PROS: checklist state (checked items, blocker notes) is mutable and saved separately without touching the main file",
    "PROS: sync-prs.sh only needs to update the lean prs array — no stage nesting to navigate",
    "PROS: a ticket with no checklist file yet just falls back to the latestUpdate/nextSteps view — zero migration cost",
    "CONS: data is now in two places; dashboard server needs to read both and merge on every request",
    "CONS: checklist.json must be kept in $JIRA_TICKETS_WORKDIR/<id>/ which is machine-local (not in the repo)"
  ],

